                        "entry_id": "c73bf233-29d7-3dcf-9c0a-24091bb0505e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Not joyous."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "445ebe26-4da8-4022-9cd4-96d058e83600",
                                "sense_id": "55cab779-be84-320d-90fe-8b739f0f5446",
                                "text": "It is from the animal joy of mechanics or peasants in their cessations from labor, or from their celebration of festivals, that the artist will select his matter of composition; not from any circumstances of unjoyous poverty or loathsome distress."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d9e27382-776a-4672-8c6d-240073debca6",
                                "sense_id": "55cab779-be84-320d-90fe-8b739f0f5446",
                                "text": "On emerging from the Old Manse, it was chiefly this strange, indolent, unjoyous attachment for my native town, that brought me to fill a place in Uncle Sam's brick edifice, when I might as well, or better, have gone somewhere else."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e62c6488-0b4a-4eb2-93a1-8f9f2a2eeffb",
                                "sense_id": "55cab779-be84-320d-90fe-8b739f0f5446",
                                "text": "In a few moments we were whirling along the straight, white road between the interminable black vineyards, and past the dilapidated homesteads of the vine-folk and wayside cafes that are scattered about this unjoyous corner of France."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
